+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry enforces the schema advertised to providers before invoking a tool executor, so malformed calls can be corrected within the existing conversation.
+
+## Contract
+
+1. `execute` rejects missing required fields with an explanatory `ToolResponse` and no executor invocation, passes accepted input and unknown properties unchanged exactly once without coercion or defaults, and preserves the unknown-tool exception. ([validated by: rejects missing input and preserves accepted input and unknown-tool behavior](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L19))
+2. Wrong types and enum violations return property paths and failed constraints without executing the tool or exposing input values in results or logs. ([validated by: rejects types and enums with safe property diagnostics in results and real logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L42))
+3. Static schemas compile at registration, invalid schemas throw an error naming the tool at registration, and ten executions reuse the compiled schema without inspecting it again. ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them across ten executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L80))
+4. Function-valued definitions validate the schema resolved for the current call, compile newly resolved schema objects, and reuse compilation when the same schema object is returned again. ([validated by: validates the current dynamic schema and caches by resolved schema identity](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L107))
+
+## Integration and delivery
+
+Rejections are tool results visible to the model on the next round; the existing five-tool-round budget bounds correction cycles, and an unknown tool name continues to throw `Unknown tool: <name>`.
+
+Use a runtime JSON Schema validator dependency, with no opt-out, type coercion, default insertion or implicit ban on additional properties; the one-line `execute` doc comment points here for the full contract.
+
+Update README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md to describe the enforced input contract and retry behavior; document the executor migration, publish a MINOR version bump, and add an npm-reader-facing CHANGELOG.md entry.
